body:
Editing an LR could fail with HTTP 400 when the modal submitted a `source` value that is not in backend-allowed enums (e.g., location text like `DRONAGIRI`). The failure surfaced in the edit form during save, even when users were updating unrelated fields.

- **Root cause**
  - `LrEditModal` sent `source` whenever the field changed, without enforcing backend constraints.
  - Backend validates `source` against `INTERNAL | PORTAL | API | EMAIL_IMPORT`, so non-enum values were rejected.

- **Change made (frontend, surgical)**
  - Normalized `source` input to uppercase before comparison.
  - Added an allowed-source guard in the modal.
  - Included `source` in PATCH payload only when:
    - it changed from current value, and
    - it matches one of the allowed backend values.
  - Otherwise, omitted `source` from update payload so other edits can proceed.

- **Code example**
  ```ts
  const normalizedSource = form.source.trim().toUpperCase();
  const currentSource = toStr(lr.source).trim().toUpperCase();

  const sourceForUpdate =
    normalizedSource &&
    normalizedSource !== currentSource &&
    ALLOWED_SOURCES.has(normalizedSource)
      ? normalizedSource
      : undefined;

  await lrApi.update(lr.id, {
    // ...
    source: sourceForUpdate,
  });
  ```
